
========================================================
HIVE PRACTICAL: DATABASE, INTERNAL TABLE AND EXTERNAL TABLE
========================================================

[STEP 1: TERMINAL]
Open Cloudera Terminal.

Start Hive:
hive


[STEP 2: HIVE SHELL]
Show existing databases:
SHOW DATABASES;

Create database:
CREATE DATABASE hiveDemoDb;

Show databases again:
SHOW DATABASES;

Create another database:
CREATE DATABASE hiveDemoDb1;

Drop the second database:
DROP DATABASE hiveDemoDb1;


[STEP 3: CREATE INTERNAL (MANAGED) TABLE]

Create an internal table:
CREATE TABLE hiveDemoDb.employee
(
    Id INT,
    Name STRING,
    Salary FLOAT
)
ROW FORMAT DELIMITED
FIELDS TERMINATED BY ',';

Describe the table:
DESCRIBE hiveDemoDb.employee;


[STEP 4: CREATE TABLE USING EXISTING TABLE SCHEMA]

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS hiveDemoDb.copy_employee
LIKE hiveDemoDb.employee;

Check the table:
DESCRIBE hiveDemoDb.copy_employee;


[STEP 5: CREATE TABLE WITH COMMENTS AND PROPERTIES]

CREATE TABLE hiveDemoDb.new_employee
(
    Id INT COMMENT 'Employee Id',
    Name STRING COMMENT 'Employee Name',
    Salary FLOAT COMMENT 'Employee Salary'
)
COMMENT 'Table Description'
TBLPROPERTIES
(
    'creator'='Gaurav Chawla',
    'created_at'='2021-11-30 11:00:00'
);

Describe the table:
DESCRIBE hiveDemoDb.new_employee;


[STEP 6: CREATE HDFS DIRECTORY]

Exit Hive:
QUIT;

[TERMINAL]
Create an HDFS directory:
hdfs dfs -mkdir -p /HiveDirectory

Check the directory:
hdfs dfs -ls /


[STEP 7: START HIVE AGAIN]

[TERMINAL]
hive

[HIVE SHELL]
Create an external table:
CREATE EXTERNAL TABLE emplist
(
    Id INT,
    Name STRING,
    Salary FLOAT
)
ROW FORMAT DELIMITED
FIELDS TERMINATED BY ','
LOCATION '/HiveDirectory';


[STEP 8: DISPLAY EXTERNAL TABLE DATA]

SELECT * FROM emplist;


[STEP 9: INSERT RECORDS INTO EXTERNAL TABLE]

Insert first employee:
INSERT INTO TABLE emplist
VALUES (11, 'John', 70000);

Insert second employee:
INSERT INTO TABLE emplist
VALUES (12, 'Robert', 80000);

Insert third employee:
INSERT INTO TABLE emplist
VALUES (13, 'Catherine', 90000);


[STEP 10: DISPLAY FINAL RECORDS]

SELECT * FROM emplist;

Expected output:

11    John       70000
12    Robert     80000
13    Catherine  90000


[STEP 11: CHECK TABLE DETAILS]

DESCRIBE emplist;

SHOW TABLES;


[STEP 12: EXIT HIVE]

QUIT;


========================================================
IMPORTANT DIFFERENCE
========================================================

INTERNAL TABLE:
- Also called Managed Table.
- Hive manages both metadata and data.
- Dropping the table deletes its data as well.

EXTERNAL TABLE:
- Created using the EXTERNAL keyword.
- Data is stored at the specified HDFS location.
- Dropping the table removes its metadata.
- The actual data remains in the HDFS directory.

